### Real-World Example 2: Provider Portal API - Code-First Migration

**Context**: Existing Provider Portal API has outdated Swagger 2.0 specification that doesn't match implementation.

**Challenge**: Specification drift has caused integration failures; need to resynchronize and adopt OpenAPI 3.0.

**Approach**: Code-first generation with validation

**Implementation**:

**Step 1: Enable OpenAPI Generation in ASP.NET Core**

```csharp
// Program.cs
builder.Services.AddSwaggerGen(options =>
{
    options.SwaggerDoc("v1", new OpenApiInfo
    {
        Title = "Gainwell Provider Portal API",
        Version = "v1",
        Description = "Provider enrollment, credentialing, and claims inquiry"
    });

    // Include XML comments for rich documentation
    var xmlFile = $"{Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly().GetName().Name}.xml";
    var xmlPath = Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, xmlFile);
    options.IncludeXmlComments(xmlPath);

    // Add Gainwell custom extensions via document filter
    options.DocumentFilter<GainwellMetadataDocumentFilter>();
});

// Custom document filter to add Gainwell extensions
public class GainwellMetadataDocumentFilter : IDocumentFilter
{
    public void Apply(OpenApiDocument swaggerDoc, DocumentFilterContext context)
    {
        swaggerDoc.Info.Extensions.Add(
            "x-gainwell-product",
            new OpenApiString("Provider+")
        );
        swaggerDoc.Info.Extensions.Add(
            "x-gainwell-phi-classification",
            new OpenApiString("Limited")
        );
    }
}
```

**Step 2: Enhance Controller Documentation**

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Provider enrollment and management operations
/// </summary>
[ApiController]
[Route("api/v1/[controller]")]
[Produces("application/json")]
public class ProvidersController : ControllerBase
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Retrieves provider details by NPI
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="npi">10-digit National Provider Identifier</param>
    /// <returns>Provider details including enrollment status</returns>
    /// <response code="200">Provider found</response>
    /// <response code="404">Provider not found</response>
    /// <response code="401">Unauthorized - authentication required</response>
    [HttpGet("{npi}")]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(ProviderDto), StatusCodes.Status200OK)]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(ErrorResponse), StatusCodes.Status404NotFound)]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(ErrorResponse), StatusCodes.Status401Unauthorized)]
    public async Task<ActionResult<ProviderDto>> GetProvider(
        [FromRoute] string npi)
    {
        // Implementation
    }
}
```

**Step 3: Export and Validate OpenAPI Specification**

```powershell
# Start API and export OpenAPI spec
dotnet run
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://localhost:5001/swagger/v1/swagger.json" `

  -OutFile "openapi/provider-portal-v1.yaml"

# Convert JSON to YAML (more readable)
npm install -g swagger2openapi
swagger2openapi openapi/provider-portal-v1.json -o openapi/provider-portal-v1.yaml

# Lint against Gainwell standards
spectral lint openapi/provider-portal-v1.yaml

# Warnings found:
# ⚠ Some properties missing examples
# ⚠ OAuth scopes not fully documented
```

**Step 4: Manual Refinement**

- Add realistic examples to generated specification
- Document OAuth scopes more clearly
- Add descriptions for complex schemas
- Commit refined specification to version control

**Step 5: Contract Testing**

```yaml
# .github/workflows/contract-tests.yml
name: Contract Tests

on:
  push:
    branches: [main, develop]

jobs:
  contract-tests:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v2

      - name: Install Dredd
        run: npm install -g dredd

      - name: Run Contract Tests
        run: |
          dredd openapi/provider-portal-v1.yaml \
            https://api-test.gainwell.com \
            --header "Authorization: Bearer ${{ secrets.TEST_TOKEN }}"
```

**Results**:

- ✅ Specification now matches implementation 100%
- ✅ CI/CD prevents future drift
- ✅ 3 partner integrations completed with generated SDKs
- ✅ Integration time reduced from 6 weeks to 2 weeks
